## Site settings: the field tables of the settings pages, the site information page, setting checks and
## cache refreshing.

config-field-registration = Registration mode
config-field-registration-help = Invite only: signing up needs a valid invite code (a member's code, or one starting with a prefix below). Open: the code is optional, but checked when given.
config-field-signup-ip-hourly-limit = Sign-ups per IP per hour
config-field-signup-ip-hourly-limit-help = Applies from the next sign-up. With Redis enabled all processes share one count; without it each process counts on its own.
config-field-invitations-enabled = Let members create new invite codes
config-field-invite-daily-limit = Invite codes each member can create per day
config-field-invite-daily-limit-help = Counts the member's own codes per calendar day in the site time zone; applies from the next code.
config-field-invite-active-limit = Unused invite codes each member can hold at once
config-field-invite-ttl-days = Invite code lifetime (days)
config-field-invite-ttl-days-help = Fixed as an expiry time when the code is issued; changes only affect new codes.
config-field-username-cooldown-days = Username change cooldown (days)
config-field-username-cooldown-days-help = Counted from the last change at the time of checking; changes apply to everyone at once.
config-field-username-history-days = Old username protection (days)
config-field-username-history-days-help = How long an old username stays reserved after a rename or account deletion; no shorter than the cooldown. Fixed as an expiry time at the rename or deletion, so changes only affect later ones.
config-field-api-enabled = Enable the member API
config-field-api-enabled-help = When off, every API request gets 403. Tokens members already created are kept and work again once it is back on. Tick and save to show the API settings below.
config-field-api-key-ttl-days = Token lifetime (days)
config-field-api-key-ttl-days-help = Written into the token when it is created; changes only affect new tokens.
config-field-api-requests-per-minute = Requests per token per minute
config-field-api-writes-per-minute = Write requests per token per minute
config-field-api-writes-per-minute-help = No more than the requests per minute.
config-field-api-auth-failures-per-5min = Failed authentications per IP per 5 minutes
config-field-api-auth-failures-per-5min-help = Past this, the IP cannot try tokens for a while.
config-field-api-max-body-kib = Request body limit (KiB)
config-field-api-max-body-kib-help = Each request is checked against the value at that time.
config-field-posting-first-day-threads = Threads allowed while new
config-field-posting-first-day-threads-help = How many threads a member can start within the "New member period" after signing up.
config-field-posting-first-day-replies = Replies allowed while new
config-field-posting-daily-threads = Threads per day
config-field-posting-daily-threads-help = After the new member period, counted per calendar day in the site time zone; no less than the threads allowed while new.
config-field-posting-daily-replies = Replies per day
config-field-posting-daily-replies-help = No less than the replies allowed while new.
config-field-posting-new-member-hours = New member period (hours)
config-field-posting-new-member-hours-help = Counted from the sign-up time at the time of checking; changes apply to existing members at once.
config-field-posting-body-max-bytes = Post body limit (bytes)
config-field-posting-body-max-bytes-help = Only applies to later submissions; older posts longer than the new limit must be shortened when edited. The hard limit is 60000 bytes (the width of the revisions column).
config-field-posting-edit-window-hours = Author edit window (hours)
config-field-posting-edit-window-hours-help = Editing, withdrawing and restoring by the author are counted from the posting time at the time of checking: changes apply to existing content at once, so posts inside the window may close and posts past it may reopen.
config-field-posting-duplicate-check = Block duplicate content
config-field-posting-duplicate-check-help = A thread or reply is refused when the same member posted the same body (identical after trimming surrounding whitespace) within the look-back time. Threads are compared with threads, replies and nested replies with replies; only the member's last 20 posts of the same kind count, and their own withdrawn posts do not.
config-field-posting-duplicate-window-minutes = Duplicate look-back (minutes)
config-field-posting-duplicate-window-minutes-help = Only used when "Block duplicate content" is on.
config-field-posting-new-member-link-block = Members in the probation period cannot post external links
config-field-posting-new-member-link-block-help = When a member still inside the probation period starts a thread, replies, edits or saves their bio, an external URL in it is refused outright, saying how many days after sign-up they can post one; it does not go to review. The body, the thread title and a news thread's source link all count, and so do URLs in links, plain text and code; this site's addresses (including subdomains) and relative addresses do not; edits only check what was added. Staff who manage the forum are exempt; for bios, administrators and global moderators.
config-field-posting-new-member-link-days = New member probation (days)
config-field-posting-new-member-link-days-help = Counted from the sign-up time at the time of checking; changes apply to existing members at once.
config-field-posting-thread-interval-seconds = Minimum time between threads (seconds)
config-field-posting-thread-interval-seconds-help = Counted from the member's previous thread; 0 for no limit.
config-field-posting-reply-interval-seconds = Minimum time between replies (seconds)
config-field-posting-reply-interval-seconds-help = Includes nested replies, counted from the member's previous reply; 0 for no limit.
config-field-posting-hourly-limit = Posts per hour
config-field-posting-hourly-limit-help = Threads and replies together over a rolling hour; 0 for no limit.
config-field-limit-message-per-minute = Private messages per member per minute
config-field-limit-message-per-minute-help = Shared by new conversations and replies.
config-field-limit-message-peer-per-minute = Private messages to one member per minute
config-field-limit-message-peer-per-minute-help = No more than the private messages per member per minute.
config-field-limit-interaction-per-minute = Likes, favorites, downvotes and member follows per minute
config-field-limit-interaction-per-hour = Likes, favorites, downvotes and member follows per hour
config-field-limit-interaction-per-hour-help = No less than the per-minute count.
config-field-limit-social-per-5min = Thread and forum follows, blocks and forum filters per 5 minutes
config-field-limit-report-daily = Reports per member per 24 hours
config-field-limit-report-daily-help = Counted in the database over a rolling 24 hours.
config-field-limit-restoration-daily = Restoration requests per member per 24 hours
config-field-governance-restoration-cooldown-days = Cooldown after a declined restoration request (days)
config-field-governance-restoration-cooldown-days-help = Counted from the last decision at the time of checking; changes apply retroactively.
config-field-governance-restoration-due-days = Restoration request handling time (days)
config-field-governance-restoration-due-days-help = Only used for display and for marking overdue requests.
config-field-governance-appeal-window-days = Appeal window after a sanction (days)
config-field-governance-appeal-window-days-help = Counted from when the sanction took effect: shortening it takes the right to appeal away from members who are still within the old window.
config-field-governance-appeal-handling-days = Appeal handling time (days)
config-field-governance-appeal-handling-days-help = Only used for display and for marking overdue appeals.
config-field-account-session-idle-days = Idle session timeout (days)
config-field-account-session-idle-days-help = How long without a visit before logging in again; renewals use the current value.
config-field-account-session-absolute-days = Maximum session length (days)
config-field-account-session-absolute-days-help = The longest a login lasts before logging in again; no shorter than the idle timeout. Sealed into the login credentials, so it only affects new logins.
config-field-account-verification-ttl-hours = Email verification link lifetime (hours)
config-field-account-verification-ttl-hours-help = Fixed as an expiry time when issued; only affects new links.
config-field-account-reset-ttl-minutes = Password reset link lifetime (minutes)
config-field-account-email-change-ttl-hours = Email change link lifetime (hours)
config-field-account-password-min-length = Minimum password length (characters)
config-field-account-password-min-length-help = Only checked when a password is set, so raising it does not lock out existing passwords; the maximum is fixed at 128 characters.
config-field-account-login-ip-per-5min = Logins per IP per 5 minutes
config-field-account-login-name-per-5min = Logins per account name per 5 minutes
config-field-account-two-factor-ip-per-5min = Two-step verifications per IP per 5 minutes
config-field-account-two-factor-ip-per-5min-help = Locking an account after repeated wrong codes follows separate fixed rules.
config-field-account-password-change-account-per-5min = Wrong current passwords per account per 5 minutes
config-field-account-password-change-account-per-5min-help = Shared by password changes and two-step verification settings; only wrong current passwords count.
config-field-account-password-change-ip-per-5min = Wrong current passwords per IP per 5 minutes
config-field-account-forgot-email-per-minute = Password resets per email per minute
config-field-account-forgot-email-per-hour = Password resets per email per hour
config-field-account-forgot-ip-per-hour = Password resets per IP per hour
config-field-account-reset-token-per-5min = Attempts per reset link per 5 minutes
config-field-account-reset-ip-per-5min = Password resets per IP per 5 minutes
config-field-display-threads-per-page = Threads per page
config-field-display-threads-per-page-help = The home page, forum pages and search results.
config-field-display-replies-per-page = Replies per page
config-field-display-replies-per-page-help = Page numbers, reply addresses and jumping to a reply on thread pages all follow it.
config-field-display-sub-replies-per-page = Nested replies per page
config-field-display-hot-days = Days counted for the sidebar's hot threads
config-field-display-hot-days-help = Threads with new replies in the last few days, ranked by reply count.
config-field-display-hot-count = Hot threads in the sidebar
config-field-display-latest-count = Latest threads in the sidebar
config-field-display-recent-members = Newest members on the home page
config-field-display-highlight-min-likes = Likes needed for a highlighted reply
config-field-display-highlight-min-likes-help = How many likes a reply on the page needs to be highlighted.
config-field-display-highlight-count = Highlighted replies
config-field-display-highlight-count-help = 0 hides highlighted replies.
config-field-display-ranks-shown = Leaderboard places shown
config-field-display-ranks-shown-help = The snapshot keeps the top 100.
config-field-display-list-thumbnails = Thumbnails in thread lists
config-field-display-list-thumbnails-help = Each row of a thread list shows the first few images of the first post (in order; GIFs and images in spoilers do not count); 0 shows none.
config-field-display-footer-metrics = Show the performance line in the footer
config-field-display-footer-metrics-help = A lightning icon, then "19.1 ms · MySQL 11 · Redis 23": the server time of the page and the queries it sent (SQLite sites say SQLite; without Redis the Redis count is left out). Shown to every visitor.
config-field-reading-list-sort = Default sort
config-field-reading-thread-view = Default reply view
config-field-reading-title-latest = Thread titles jump to the latest reply
config-field-reading-title-new-tab = Open thread titles in a new tab
config-field-reading-avatar-shape = Default avatar shape
config-field-debug-panel = Debug panel at the bottom of admin pages
config-field-debug-panel-help = When on, every page an administrator opens lists this request's SQL, Redis commands, timings and in-process cache use at the bottom; other visitors are not affected. The old deployment setting app_debug and the APP_DEBUG environment variable are no longer used.
config-field-maintenance-outbox-retention-days = Notification and mail event retention (days)
config-field-maintenance-outbox-retention-days-help = How long sent content notifications and mail events are kept. Mail written to files (mail/*.eml) and its prepared copy are deleted with their event.
config-field-maintenance-prepared-mail-retention-days = Prepared mail retention (days)
config-field-maintenance-prepared-mail-retention-days-help = How long sent or cancelled prepared mail (mail/prepared/*.eml) is kept, at most as long as its event.
config-field-maintenance-request-retention-days = Request key retention (days)
config-field-maintenance-request-retention-days-help = How long the request keys of posts and interactions are remembered to detect replays; after that, a submission with the same key counts as a new request. At least 7 days: too short and client retries count as new requests, posting twice.
config-field-link-applications = Accept friend link applications
config-field-link-applications-help = When off, the application page says applications are closed and the directory and home page show no way to apply; existing applications and links stay, and review continues as usual.
config-field-links-home-count = Links in the home page sidebar
config-field-links-home-count-help = Links marked "Show on home page", the first few by sort value.
config-field-links-live-per-member = Links each account can have pending or shown at once
config-field-links-live-per-member-help = Links already over a new limit are not taken down.
config-field-links-reject-cooldown-days = Cooldown before reapplying after a rejection (days)
config-field-links-reject-cooldown-days-help = Counted from the rejection at the time of checking.
config-field-links-min-account-days = Days since sign-up before applying
config-field-links-min-account-days-help = Administrators are exempt.
config-field-links-apply-per-hour = Applications per account per hour
config-field-links-apply-ip-per-hour = Applications per IP per hour
config-field-links-apply-ip-per-hour-help = No less than the applications per account per hour.
config-field-growth-thread = Starting a thread
config-field-growth-reply = A valid reply
config-field-growth-reply-help = Replies and nested replies both count.
config-field-growth-like = Each like received
config-field-growth-digest = Thread marked as featured
config-field-growth-accept = Reply accepted for a bounty
config-field-growth-link-level = Level needed to post external links
config-field-growth-link-level-help = A level number, 1 for no limit; the new member probation applies as well, to the same posts and bios. Staff who manage the forum being posted to are exempt; for bios, administrators and global moderators.
config-field-growth-invite-level = Level needed to create invite codes
config-field-growth-invite-level-help = A level number, 1 for no limit. Staff are exempt; batch creation in the admin area and invite code prefixes are not affected.
config-field-growth-activity-level = Level needed to start red packets and lotteries
config-field-growth-activity-level-help = A level number, 1 for no limit; joining other members' activities is not affected. Staff who manage the forum being posted to are exempt.
config-field-ranks-refresh-seconds = Leaderboard refresh interval (seconds)
config-field-ranks-refresh-seconds-help = How often the leaderboard snapshot is recomputed; the background task reads this value again on every round.
config-field-invite-prefixes = Invite code prefixes
config-field-invite-prefixes-help = One per line, at most 50, no duplicates, each 2–6 letters, digits, underscores or hyphens, case-sensitive. Any invite code starting with one of the prefixes can be used to sign up (with the prefix hoph, hophoto43saf242 works); such codes are not used up, can be reused and count against no member's invite allowance. Delete a line to retire that prefix. Leave empty to turn this off.
config-field-growth-levels = Level thresholds
config-field-growth-levels-help = Comma-separated integers, starting at 0 and strictly increasing, 1 to 20 levels; saved and checked together with the level names.
config-field-growth-level-names = Level names
config-field-growth-level-names-help = One per line, matching the thresholds one to one, each 1 to 20 characters; leave empty to show the default names in the site language (such as "Level 1").
config-section-registration = Registration & permissions
config-section-registration-intro = How members sign up, invite codes members can create, invite code prefixes, usernames and the member API.
config-section-api = Member API
config-section-api-intro = Applies while the member API is on: token lifetime, rate limits and the request body limit.
config-section-posting = Posting
config-section-posting-intro = Posting allowances, the body limit, the author edit window and content rules for ordinary members. Administrators have no allowances; administrators, global moderators and the moderators and trainee moderators of the forum (or a parent forum) are exempt from these rules. Frozen accounts are still blocked.
config-section-rates = Rates
config-section-rates-intro = Posting intervals and posts per hour are counted in the database within the posting transaction; private messages, interactions and social actions go through rate limits, with the window in their names. With Redis enabled all processes share one count; without it each process counts on its own. The next check uses the new values.
config-section-governance = Reports, restorations and appeals
config-section-governance-intro = Reports and restoration requests skip the read-only gate and are accepted while the forum is read-only.
config-section-sessions = Sessions and links
config-section-sessions-intro = Loosening these weakens account security directly; each has a hard minimum.
config-section-account-limits = Rate limits
config-section-account-limits-intro = The window is in each name. With Redis enabled all processes share one count; without it each process counts on its own.
config-section-display = Lists and replies
config-section-display-intro = After changing the number per page, old links with page numbers land on other content.
config-section-reading = Site default reading preferences
config-section-reading-intro = Used for anonymous visitors, and for members who chose "Follow the site" for an item under "My › Reading preferences".
config-section-maintenance = Maintenance
config-section-maintenance-intro = The debug panel and how long records are kept. Retention cleanup runs once a minute, at most 500 records of each kind per round.
config-section-link-rules = Application rules
config-section-growth = Growth points
config-section-growth-intro = Points are written into a post when it is made, so changes only affect later posts; levels are computed when read, so everyone shows the new thresholds at once.
config-page-registration-summary = Registration modes, invite codes and prefixes, usernames and the member API
config-page-posting-summary = Posting allowances and content rules, rate limits, and the deadlines for reports, restorations and appeals
config-page-account-summary = Session lengths, link lifetimes, the password length and login rate limits
config-page-parameters-summary = Paging of lists and replies, sidebar counts, the footer performance line and the site default reading preferences
config-page-maintenance-summary = The debug panel and how long records are kept
config-option-registration-closed = Closed
config-option-registration-invite = Invite only
config-option-registration-open = Open
# A number field got something else; $field is the field's label.
config-error-integer = “{ $field }” must be a whole number
config-error-levels-integers = Level thresholds must be comma-separated integers
config-prefix-home = Home page
config-prefix-login = Log in
config-prefix-admin = Admin area
config-prefix-settings = This settings page
config-prefix-feed = Feed
config-prefix-sitemap = Sitemap
config-prefix-health = Health check
# How a deployment at the root path is written where a path prefix would go.
config-prefix-root = the root path /
config-site-description = Site information, read-only mode, the forum URL and time settings
config-prefix-type-confirm = Type confirm (in lowercase) in the confirmation box, then save.
# $from and $to are the old and new path prefixes (or config-prefix-root).
config-prefix-change = The forum URL's path is changing from { $from } to { $to }. This takes effect as soon as you save: every page under the old path (this admin page included) returns 404 at once, and the whole site does if nginx is not changed too. When you are sure, type confirm below and save again.
config-search-description = Search engine indexing, the site description, robots, site verification, feeds and cache lifetimes
# Shown after a successful save when robots says Disallow: / for all crawlers.
config-robots-blocks-all = robots.txt has "Disallow: /" under "User-agent: *": search engines will stop crawling the whole site. To pause indexing only, turn indexing off instead.
config-cache-refreshed-shared = This process's cache was cleared and the other processes were told to clear theirs.
config-cache-refreshed = The process cache was cleared; the database is read again from the next request.
# $detail is why Redis could not be reached.
config-cache-refresh-unpublished = This process's cache was cleared, but the other processes could not be told ({ $detail }). They refresh after their own cache lifetime; try again once Redis is back.
config-saved = Settings saved.
config-save = Save settings
config-prefix-heading = Confirm changing the forum URL's path
# $from_html and $to_html are the old and new path prefixes.
config-prefix-from-to = The path changes from { $from_html } to { $to_html }. Common pages now and after saving:
config-prefix-page = Page
config-prefix-now = Now
config-prefix-after = After saving
config-prefix-nginx = nginx configuration for the new path (passed through as is; the forum strips the path prefix itself; the port is this service's listen address):
config-prefix-redirect = Redirect the old path to the new one with a 301 (sent emails, external links and search engines rely on it):
config-prefix-step-nginx = Add the nginx configuration for the new path first and keep the old one;
config-prefix-step-save = Type confirm on this page and save; the old addresses return 404 right away, this page included;
config-prefix-step-check = Open the admin area at the new address and check that it works;
config-prefix-step-root = Before handing the old root path to another program, make sure no old links are still in use.
config-prefix-step-redirect = Change the old path in nginx to the 301 above, and decide later when to remove it.
config-prefix-to-root = After moving back to the root path, every request to the root goes to the forum; move any other program on the root path away first.
# $command_html is the command that restores the old forum URL.
config-prefix-rescue = If it goes wrong and you cannot reach the admin area, run { $command_html } in the project directory on the server to restore the old address; it takes effect at once.
config-prefix-confirm-label = Type confirm to save
config-site-heading = Site information
config-site-intro = The site name, contact details and read-only mode. Registration, invites and the member API are under "Registration & permissions"; search engine indexing and the site description are under "Search & performance".
config-site-name = Site name
# $product is the product name shown when the field is empty.
config-site-name-help = Used in title suffixes, share cards, feeds, the manifest and emails; leave empty to show { $product }.
config-brand-text = Header brand text
config-brand-text-help = The text at the top left of the header; leave empty to show { $product }. Other domains use their own site names.
config-credit-name = Points name
# $default is the language's default word.
config-credit-name-help = Leave empty to show "{ $default }" in the site language.
config-index-name = Activity index name
config-index-name-help = What the sidebar statistics call this week's contributions; leave empty to show "{ $default }" in the site language.
config-contact-email = Contact email
config-contact-email-help = Shown below the text of the contact page /contact; leave empty to hide it.
config-read-only = Read-only forum
config-read-only-help = While read-only, only actions that are publicly visible or bring in new accounts are blocked: posting, replying, editing and withdrawing, private messages, changing public profiles and avatars, likes, votes, accepting bounty answers, uploading attachments, signing up and creating invite codes. Favorites, follows, blocks, check-ins, cancelling one's own attachments, revoking invite codes, reading notifications and notification preferences, profile visibility, account security, API tokens, reports and appeals, data requests and admin moderation work as usual.
config-read-only-message = Read-only notice
config-url-heading = Forum URL
config-url-intro = The forum URL used in external links; when the forum lives under a sub-path (such as https://demo.com/bbs), include the path here.
# $current is the address derived from this request.
config-url-help = External links (canonical, share cards, the sitemap, feeds and emails) all use it. When empty, pages derive it from this request's Host (now { $current }; a reverse proxy must pass the original Host through); emails and background tasks have no request, so emails with links cannot be sent while it is empty. Fill it in on production and test sites. Under a sub-path include the path; each path segment may only use lowercase letters, digits and -.
# $path_html is config-url-path-differs in bold; $command_html is the rescue command.
config-url-note = The scheme and domain only affect canonical URLs, the sitemap, URLs returned by the API and links in emails. They do not change the address the server listens on, nor cookies or the same-origin policy, so a wrong value only makes links point to the wrong place. { $path_html }: it decides which path the forum lives under and takes effect as soon as you save, and pages under the old path (the admin area included) return 404 at once. So a path change goes through a confirmation first, and nginx must be changed too. If it goes wrong, run { $command_html } on the server to recover.
config-url-path-differs = The path is different
config-url-rescue-command = gono-forum-cli set-site-url OLD_URL
config-time-heading = Time
config-time-intro = Times are always stored in UTC. The site time zone decides how pages show times, which time zone times typed into forms are read in, and when "daily" and "weekly" start.
config-time-zone = Site time zone
config-time-zone-help = Time zones with the same offset behave the same and are merged into one option; none use daylight saving time.
config-date-format = Date format
config-date-format-locale = Follow the language
config-clock24 = Use the 24-hour clock
config-relative-time = Show recent times as "3 hours ago"
config-relative-hours = Relative time range (hours)
config-relative-hours-help = Older times fall back to absolute times.
# $credit is the site's name for its points.
config-time-note = Check-ins, the daily limits of { $credit } rewards and tips, the daily allowances for posts and invite codes, the daily upload allowance and "earned today" all settle per calendar day in the site time zone; the sidebar's "contributors this week" starts at midnight on Monday in the site time zone. The next settlement after saving uses the new time zone; on the day of a change the day boundary moves, so members may check in one extra time.
config-upcoming = Coming later
config-upcoming-intro = These settings will move to this page in a later version; until then the current rules apply.
# The summary under the heading of a settings page; $summary is the page's summary.
config-page-summary = { $summary }.
config-seo-heading = SEO
config-seo-saved = SEO settings saved.
config-seo-intro = Search engine indexing, the site description, robots.txt and site verification. The site name (the home page title and the suffix of every title) is under "Site settings".
config-seo-indexing = Let search engines index public pages
config-seo-indexing-help = When off, robots.txt is always "Disallow: /", the sitemap is empty and pages are marked not to be indexed. Keep test sites unindexed.
config-seo-description = Site description
config-seo-description-help = The description of the home page, search pages and feeds, and the fallback when a forum description or thread summary is empty. Search results usually show only the first 80–120 characters; at most 500.
config-seo-robots-help = Served as is while indexing is on, with "Sitemap: site URL/sitemap.xml" added at the end (no need to write it); not used while indexing is off. At most 100 lines and 4000 characters; directives are not checked. robots is only a convention for well-behaved crawlers, not access control; "Disallow: /" makes search engines stop crawling the whole site.
config-seo-robots-merge = To merge into the domain root's robots.txt
config-seo-robots-merge-help = The forum lives under a sub-path, and crawlers only read /robots.txt at the domain root, so the forum's own file has no effect. Merge the text above (rules already carry the path prefix, sitemap included) into the domain root's robots.txt; after changing the rules or the indexing switch, merge the new text again after saving.
config-seo-verification = Site verification
# $meta_html is a sample meta element (config-seo-meta-name, config-seo-meta-value); $reserved lists the meta names this site already outputs.
config-seo-verification-help = One "name=value" per line, output as { $meta_html } on page 1 of the home page only, whatever the indexing switch says; at most 10 lines. Only fill in the verification names and codes search platforms give you, such as google-site-verification, msvalidate.01 (Bing), baidu-site-verification, 360-site-verification, sogou_site_verification and yandex-verification; DNS TXT record verification needs nothing here. Names may only use letters, digits, dots, underscores and hyphens, and cannot be one this site already outputs: { $reserved }. Values may only use letters, digits, underscores and hyphens.
config-seo-save = Save SEO settings
config-feed-heading = Feeds
