config-cache-heading = Cache
config-cache-saved = Cache settings saved.
# $credit is the site's name for its points.
config-cache-intro = Site settings and navigation, policies, brand images, { $credit } rules, friend links, forums, the moderator roster, the pin index, honor groups and the domain table keep a copy in each process's memory; saving in the admin area takes effect in this process at once.
config-cache-intro-shared = Site settings and navigation, policies, brand images, { $credit } rules, friend links, forums, the moderator roster, the pin index, honor groups and the domain table keep a copy in each process's memory; saving in the admin area takes effect in this process at once, and the other processes are told.
config-cache-ttl = In-process cache lifetime (seconds)
config-cache-ttl-help = Admin saves take effect without it; it only bounds changes made around the admin area (editing the database by hand, the command line), at most a day. 0 turns the in-process cache off and every request reads the database; set it to 0 when profiling SQL. Signed-in members' reading preferences and forum filters are cached for at most 300 seconds.
config-cache-ttl-help-shared = Admin saves take effect without it; it only bounds changes made around the admin area (editing the database by hand, the command line), at most a day. 0 turns the in-process cache off and every request reads the database; set it to 0 when profiling SQL. Signed-in members' reading preferences and forum filters are cached in Redis for at most 300 seconds.
config-cache-page-ttl = Reply cache lifetime (seconds)
config-cache-page-ttl-help = Replies and rendered post bodies seen by anonymous visitors.
config-cache-no-redis = Redis is not enabled, so this has no effect.
config-cache-list-ttl = List cache lifetime (seconds)
config-cache-list-ttl-help = Anonymous lists, the sidebar's hot and latest threads, and feeds.
config-cache-statistics = Site statistics cache time (seconds)
config-cache-statistics-help = The sidebar's thread, reply and participant counts and the newest member anonymous visitors see refresh in steps of this length.
config-cache-forum-statistics = Forum statistics cache time (seconds)
config-cache-forum-statistics-help = Thread counts and today's posts on the forum directory /forums and the admin forum list refresh in steps of this length.
config-cache-save = Save cache settings
config-cache-refresh = Refresh caches
config-cache-refresh-intro = Clears the process cache; the database is read again from the next request. Changes saved in the admin area do not need it; click it once after editing the database by hand or changing settings from the command line.
config-cache-refresh-intro-shared = Clears the process cache; the database is read again from the next request, and the other processes are told to clear theirs too. Changes saved in the admin area do not need it; click it once after editing the database by hand or changing settings from the command line.
